3. Permitted Uses (General)

3.1 Use. Any person or entity may use the Work for any lawful purpose,
including Commercial Use, subject to Section 8 (Commercial Use of Official
Compiled Binaries) and Section 9 (Internal Use of Modified Versions) below.

3.2 Modification. Any person or entity may Modify the Work, including
privately, for any lawful purpose.

4. Non-Commercial Redistribution

A person or entity may engage in Non-Commercial Redistribution of a Fork, in
Source Form, without obtaining a commercial license under Section 7, provided
that all of the following conditions are met:

4.1 The Fork contains at least one Material Modification (as defined in
Section 1.6);

4.2 The distributor preserves all copyright, license, and attribution notices
required under Section 10;

4.3 The distributor clearly identifies the Fork as modified from the original
Work, and identifies, at a reasonably discoverable level of detail, the nature
of the modifications made;

4.4 The Fork, and its distribution, complies with Section 11 (Project Name and
Trademark); and

4.5 The distribution does not constitute Commercial Distribution as defined in
Section 1.12.

Non-Commercial Redistribution under this Section may be made free of charge
or, where consistent with Section 1.12, in exchange for reasonable costs
unrelated to commercializing the Work itself (for example, reasonable
reproduction or media costs), provided this is not used as a mechanism to
circumvent Section 1.12.

5. Commercial Distribution and Commercial Licensing

5.1 Permission Required. Commercial Distribution of the Work, or of a
Materially Modified Fork, requires the prior express written permission of the
Licensor in the form of a separate commercial license agreement ("Commercial
License"). This requirement applies based on the intent and nature of the
distribution activity, not solely on whether payment has already occurred at
the time of distribution.

5.2 Process. A person or entity intending to engage in Commercial Distribution
must contact the Licensor at morphedstill@gmail.com / blsnmrvn004@gmail.com
with a description of the intended use, before engaging in that Commercial
Distribution.

5.3 Discretion. The Licensor may approve or refuse any request for a
Commercial License at its sole discretion, and is under no obligation to
provide a reason for its decision, to negotiate, or to grant approval.

5.4 Terms. A Commercial License, if granted, will be a separate written
agreement between the Licensor and the commercial licensee. It may specify,
among other things: a licensing fee; permitted versions of the Work; permitted
methods of distribution; attribution and linking requirements; support
obligations; duration; termination conditions; and other terms negotiated
between the parties. Payment of a fee alone does not grant permission to
engage in Commercial Distribution unless and until a Commercial License has
been agreed.

5.5 No Effect on Sections 3, 4, 8, and 9. Nothing in this Section 5 restricts
uses expressly permitted under Sections 3, 4, 8, or 9 of this License.

6. Modification and Attribution Requirements for Redistributed Forks

Any redistribution of a Fork under Section 4 (Non-Commercial Redistribution)
or under a Commercial License (Section 5), unless the Commercial License
states otherwise, must include, in the Fork's README file (or equivalent
primary documentation) and in any other location where users would reasonably
encounter information about the Fork:

6.1 Preservation of the Work's original copyright notice(s) and the full text
of this License, in the Source Form of the Fork;

6.2 A clear, visible statement that the Fork is based on, or forked from,
sceneform;

6.3 A link to the original repository of the Work:
https://github.com/arvdevable/sceneform; and

6.4 A link to the Licensor: https://github.com/arvdevable/sceneform /
morphedstill@gmail.com / blsnmrvn004@gmail.com.

A Commercial License granted under Section 5 may specify additional or
modified attribution and linking requirements applicable to that commercial
licensee, which will govern in place of this Section 6 to the extent they
conflict.

7. Commercial License Terms (Reference)

Terms for Commercial Licenses are negotiated on a case-by-case basis between
the Licensor and the commercial licensee pursuant to Section 5. This License
does not itself grant Commercial Distribution rights; it establishes the
process and conditions under which such rights may be separately obtained.

8. Commercial Use of Official Compiled Binaries

Commercial Use of an Official Compiled Binary (as defined in Section 1.4) is
permitted without obtaining a Commercial License. For example, an individual
or organization may obtain an Official Compiled Binary of the Work and use it
internally in a commercial business without that use, by itself, requiring a
Commercial License.

This Section 8 does not permit Commercial Distribution of the Official
Compiled Binary itself in a manner that would otherwise constitute Commercial
Distribution under Section 1.12 — for example, repackaging and reselling the
Official Compiled Binary as part of a competing commercial product without
permission remains subject to Section 5.

9. Internal Use of Modified Versions

A person or entity operating a business may Modify the Work and use that
Modified version internally, including for commercial/business purposes,
without obtaining a Commercial License, provided that the Modified version is
not distributed to third parties in a manner that would constitute Commercial
Distribution under Section 1.12. Internal Use does not include hosting a
Materially Modified version as a paid or for-profit network-accessible service
to third parties, which is addressed under Section 1.12(d).

10. Attribution and Notices (General)

In addition to the Fork-specific requirements of Section 6, any distribution of
the Work, in Source Form or Object Form, must retain all copyright, patent,
trademark, and attribution notices that were present in the Source Form of
the Work, except that notices that do not pertain to any part of the Derivative
Work may be omitted from that Derivative Work.

11. Project Name and Trademark

11.1 No Registered Mark. As of the effective date of this License, sceneform
and any associated logos are not represented as registered trademarks. This
Section establishes contractual naming and branding conditions under this
License; it does not itself create or waive any trademark rights the Licensor
may hold or later acquire.

11.2 Permitted Use of Original Name/Logo. A Fork may use the name "sceneform"
or the Licensor's associated logo, including in forms such as "sceneform
Community Edition," "sceneform Fork," or "sceneform by [Fork Author],"
automatically under this License, provided that the Fork:

* (a) clearly and prominently identifies itself as unofficial, independent, and
  not published by the Licensor;

* (b) does not state or imply that it is endorsed, sponsored, authorized, or
  officially released by the Licensor; and

* (c) complies with the attribution requirements of Section 6.

11.3 Different Name. A Fork may instead adopt an entirely different name
unrelated to sceneform. Regardless of naming choice, the attribution
requirements of Section 6 remain mandatory.

11.4 No Implication of Endorsement. No provision of this License shall be
construed as permission to state or imply Licensor's endorsement, sponsorship,
affiliation with, or approval of any Fork, product, or service, beyond what
is expressly stated in a separate written agreement with the Licensor.

