13. Termination

13.1 Cure Period. Except as provided in Section 13.2, if a person or entity
breaches this License, the Licensor will provide notice of the breach, and
that person or entity will have forty (40) days from such notice to cure the
breach. If not cured within that period, the License granted to that person
or entity under this License terminates automatically at the end of the cure
period.

13.2 Immediate Termination. The License granted to a person or entity
terminates immediately, without a cure period, upon:

* (a) engaging in Commercial Distribution without the required Commercial
  License or Licensor approval under Section 5; or

* (b) violating Section 11 by falsely representing a Fork as official,
  authorized, sponsored, or endorsed by the Licensor.

The Licensor may, at its discretion, also treat other serious violations of
this License as immediate-termination events where warranted by the nature of
the violation.

13.3 Effect of Termination. Upon termination of a person's or entity's rights
under this License:

* (a) that person or entity must cease all further use, reproduction, and
  distribution of the Work and any Fork under their control, and must take
  down or remove copies they directly control or host (including, for
  example, self-hosted deployments or repositories under their control);

* (b) copies of the Work or a Fork already distributed to, and outside the
  control of, the terminated party (e.g., already in the hands of third-party
  recipients) are not required to be recalled or removed, and this License
  does not purport to terminate rights previously and validly granted to those
  independent third-party recipients with respect to copies already in their
  possession;

* (c) termination applies only to the person or entity that committed the
  violation, and does not, by itself, terminate the rights of other, unrelated
  recipients of the Work or of independently distributed Forks who are not
  themselves in breach.

13.4 Survival. Sections 1 (Definitions), 12.2 (Ownership Retained), 15
(Copyright and Ownership), 16 (Patent Rights — solely with respect to the
automatic termination provision in 16.2), 17 (Warranty Disclaimer), 18
(Limitation of Liability), 20 (Governing Law and Jurisdiction), and this
Section 13.4 survive termination of this License.

